    {
      "n": 2,
      "title": "Advantages of Fermentation",
      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIa-j-12",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Explain the advantages of fermentation.</li><li>Describe situations where fermentation is beneficial.</li><li>Relate fermentation to real-world applications.</li><li>Compare fermentation to aerobic respiration.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>Fermentation</strong> — anaerobic ATP production.</li><li><strong>Rapid ATP</strong> — fast but low yield.</li><li><strong>Applications</strong> — food, industry, medicine.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Advantages of Fermentation</h4><ul><li>Works without oxygen — useful in low-O₂ environments</li><li>Very fast — quick ATP for short bursts</li><li>Regenerates NAD⁺ to keep glycolysis going</li><li>Used in food production (bread, cheese, yogurt, beer)</li><li>Used in biofuel production (ethanol)</li></ul><h4>B. Where It Happens</h4><ul><li>Muscle cells during intense exercise</li><li>Yeast in fermentation vats</li><li>Bacteria in yogurt and cheese</li></ul><h4>C. Real-Life Examples</h4><ul><li>Sprinting (lactic acid)</li><li>Bread rising (CO₂ from yeast)</li><li>Yogurt fermentation (lactic acid bacteria)</li></ul>",
      "activity1": {
        "timeLimit": 90,
        "badgeId": "ferm-master",
