      "competency": "STEM_BIO11/12-IIa-j-12",
      "content": "<h3>🎯 Learning Objectives</h3><ul><li>Explain the advantages of aerobic respiration.</li><li>Compare ATP yield to fermentation.</li><li>Describe why most organisms use aerobic respiration.</li><li>Analyze trade-offs between aerobic and anaerobic strategies.</li></ul><h3>🔑 Key Concepts</h3><ul><li><strong>High ATP yield</strong> — 32 ATP per glucose.</li><li><strong>Complete oxidation</strong> — glucose → CO₂ + H₂O.</li><li><strong>Sustained energy</strong> — supports long-term activity.</li></ul><h3>📚 Lesson Content</h3><h4>A. Advantages of Aerobic Respiration</h4><ul><li>Produces ~32 ATP per glucose (16× fermentation)</li><li>Sustains long-term activity (endurance exercise)</li><li>Powers large organisms with high energy needs</li><li>Allows complex multicellular life</li></ul><h4>B. Comparison Table</h4><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Fermentation</th><th>Aerobic</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>O₂</td><td>Not required</td><td>Required</td></tr><tr><td>ATP</td><td>2</td><td>~32</td></tr><tr><td>Speed</td><td>Fast</td><td>Slower</td></tr><tr><td>Sustainability</td><td>Short bursts</td><td>Long-term</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Cytoplasm</td><td>Cytoplasm + mitochondria</td></tr></tbody></table>",
